      2
    ],
    "text": "Naturally a non-spa-style bathtub without a secondary heating system and circulating jet will get noticeably cooler after being filled with hot water. The water lose heat both to the air and to the bathtub. One want to keep warm by adding a constant trickle of hot water from the faucet. To handle fluid\u2019s overflowing, the bathtub is designed in such a way that when the tub reached its capacity, excess water escapes through an overflow drain."
  },
